heck from D17, per spec's own row split (\"D17\n66\t... repeated bound = exhaustion\" vs. \"D18 ... attempt bound = exhaustion\").\n67\t\n68\t## Denominator trace (D16 / D22, `acceptance.compute_unit_denominator`)\n69\t\n70\tRecomputed identically by D16 (before repair) and D22 (immediately before\n71\tminting an accepted receipt) off whatever heads are *current* at call time.\n72\tCategories enforced this generation: source admission (sha256-resolved),\n73\tdomain check set (`DOMAIN_CHECK_IDS`, matched by current head hash), content\n74\tcheck set (`CONTENT_CHECK_IDS`, matched by current head hash), visual join\n75\tresult, page inventory + inspection set (exact page count, all PASS), one\n76\tindependent unit review with every blocking finding's `category` mapped\n77\tthrough the code-owned `owner_for_review_category()` table (never trusted\n78\tverbatim from the model), and repair-request closure (no request left\n79\tunresolved). `test_removing_or_failing_any_single_member_makes_d22_reject`\n80\tindependently removes/fails each of the five owner-bearing categories and\n81\tconfirms D22 raises every time; `test_staling_the_content_head_makes_d22_reject`\n82\tconfirms a check recorded against a superseded head is invisible to the\n83\treduction (stale evidence cannot pass) without needing to delete anything —\n84\t`compute_unit_denominator` only counts a check whose `head_hash` equals the\n85\t*current* head.\n86\t\n87\tDocumented, not silently assumed, scope limit: this generation's denominator\n88\ttreats the append-only evidence/log layer and the LangGraph checkpoint layer\n89\tas structurally present (state reducers already enforce their shape) rather\n90\tthan independently re-auditing their hash chain from inside D22 (spec\n91\tsection 13.1 items 13-14). `acceptance.py`'s module docstring records this so\n92\ta future generation tightens it rather than rediscovering the gap.\n93\t\n94\t## Real-D98 traces (TEST 9)\n95\t\n96\t`tests/runtime/test_plan26_repair_