{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01ERzZe9n7QWumugiZMn3fKe","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t\"\"\"Targeted repair engine: D17-D21 of spec section 6.2 and section 12.\n2\t\n3\tOwns finding classification, one-partition-member repair planning, deterministic\n4\tvs. model routing, boundary-checked admission, and retest dispatch. Shared by the\n5\tunit repair cycle here and reused by the workbook repair cycle N32 builds over\n6\t`repair_requests`-shaped state (spec section 12's boundary/diff/invalidation-DAG\n7\tmachinery is one engine, not a per-caller copy).\n8\t\n9\tNone of this module's functions carry a `NODE_CATALOGUE` row: D16-D23 are not\n10\tregistered as graph nodes yet (that registration is N32's write, once\n11\t`workbook.py` exists to dispatch alongside them), so these are plain, narrowly\n12\tscoped `(state, runtime_context) -> update` callables in the same shape N23's\n13\t`model_nodes.py` uses for D90/D91 -- state-projected by hand, not by\n14\t`nodes.deterministic_node()`. A future registration step binds them to their\n15\tcatalogue rows without changing this module.\n16\t\n17\tEvery finding this engine classifies is normalized to spec section 12's\n18\t`{finding_id, evidence_key, owner, boundary, parent_hash, fingerprint}` shape.\n19\tOwner is never trusted from a model: D08/D09/D12/D14 stamp `owner` themselves\n20\t(code-owned), and a model review's own `category` field is deliberately never\n21\tread as an owner -- `owner_for_review_category()` is the one place a category\n22\tstring is mapped to the five-owner vocabulary, and an unmapped category is a\n23\tsystem fault, not a silent guess.\n24\t\"\"\"\n25\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"2e2dab0f-1896-47a1-b9f2-90f9a7c4d3fd","uuid":"452250f2-df74-4784-a866-3f0791796fe7","timestamp":"2026-08-12T23:00:39.432Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/filipepinto/Projects/curriculum_builder/.plan26-run/plan26/attempts/N31_REPAIR_ACCEPTANCE/attempt-20260812T225852.833620Z-cb71442f0e/repo/runtime/langgraph_factory/repair.py","content":"\"\"\"Targeted repair engine: D17-D21 of spec section 6.2 and section 12.\n\nOwns finding classification, one-partition-member repair planning, deterministic\nvs. model routing, boundary-checked admission, and retest dispatch. Shared by the\nunit repair cycle here and reused by the workbook repair cycle N32 builds over\n`repair_requests`-shaped state (spec section 12's boundary/diff/invalidation-DAG\nmachinery is one engine, not a per-caller copy).\n\nNone of this module's functions carry a `NODE_CATALOGUE` row: D16-D23 are not\nregistered as graph nodes yet (that registration is N32's write, once\n`workbook.py` exists to dispatch alongside them), so these are plain, narrowly\nscoped `(state, runtime_context) -> update` callables in the same shape N23's\n`model_nodes.py` uses for D90/D91 -- state-projected by hand, not by\n`nodes.deterministic_node()`. A future registration step binds them to their\ncatalogue rows without changing this module.\n\nEvery finding this engine classifies is normalized to spec section 12's\n`{finding_id, evidence_key, owner, boundary, parent_hash, fingerprint}` shape.\nOwner is never trusted from a model: D08/D09/D12/D14 stamp `owner` themselves\n(code-owned), and a model review's own `category` field is deliberately never\nread as an owner -- `owner_for_review_category()` is the one place a category\nstring is mapped to the five-owner vocabulary, and an unmapped category is a\nsystem fault, not a silent guess.\n\"\"\"\n","numLines":25,"startLine":1,"totalLines":1057}}}
