{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01GXgUoMzVkyRKjpsi7vtzo9","type":"tool_result","content":"100\t    \"runtime.langgraph_factory.acceptance\",\n101\t)\n102\t\n103\tPLACEHOLDER_NAME_MARKERS: tuple[str, ...] = (\n104\t    \"stub\",\n105\t    \"placeholder\",\n106\t    \"fake\",\n107\t    \"dummy\",\n108\t    \"mock\",\n109\t    \"sample\",\n110\t    \"example\",\n111\t    \"todo\",\n112\t    \"noop\",\n113\t    \"test\",\n114\t)\n115\t\n116\tPLACEHOLDER_SOURCE_MARKERS: tuple[str, ...] = (\n117\t    \"raise NotImplementedError\",\n118\t    \"TODO: implement\",\n119\t    \"placeholder implementation\",\n120\t)\n121\t\n122\t# Registered here, wired by a later graph node. A node that is neither wired by\n123\t# the skeleton/unit-path tables `_validate_topology` inspects nor declared here\n124\t# fails the build: silence about an unwired node is how a topology gap becomes\n125\t# a silent halt at runtime.\n126\t#\n127\t# D16 and D17 need no row: once their bodies are members of `available`, they\n128\t# are reached as real *destinations* of already-wired `unit_graph.UNIT_BRANCHES`\n129\t# sources (D08/D09/D12/D14/D91 -> D17, M05 -> D16 -- the six rows `unit_graph\n130\t# .DEFERRED_EDGES` names), so `_validate_topology`'s own `wired` set already\n131\t# contains them. D18-D23 are reached only from *inside* the unit repair cycle\n132\t# itself (D17 -> D18 -> ... -> D21 -> D16, D22 -> D23 -> D05), which is wired by\n133\t# `acceptance.register_unit_repair_path` (via `register_unit_repair_topology`,\n134\t# called after `register_skeleton` returns) rather than by any table\n135\t# `_validate_topology` reads -- so they are declared deferred here for the same\n136\t# reason M06/M07/M08 are: really wired, by a registration step this function\n137\t# does not itself see.\n138\tDEFERRED_TOPOLOGY: Mapping[str, str] = {\n139\t    \"D18_PLAN_TARGETED_UNIT_REPAIR\": \"N31_REPAIR_ACCEPTANCE\",\n140\t    \"D19_ROUTE_UNIT_REPAIR\": \"N31_REPAIR_ACCEPTANCE\",\n141\t    \"D20_ADMIT_UNIT_REPAIR\": \"N31_REPAIR_ACCEPTANCE\",\n142\t    \"D21_RETEST_REQUIRED_DESCENDANTS\": \"N31_REPAIR_ACCEPTANCE\",\n143\t    \"D22_ACCEPT_UNIT\": \"N31_REPAIR_ACCEPTANCE\",\n144\t    \"D23_CHECKPOINT_ACCEPTED_UNIT\": \"N31_REPAIR_ACCEPTANCE\",\n145\t    \"M06_REPAIR_NAMED_UNIT_ARTIFACT\": \"N31_REPAIR_ACCEPTANCE\",\n146\t    \"M07_REVIEW_ACTUAL_WORKBOOK\": \"N32_WORKBOOK_TERMINALS\",\n147\t    \"M08_REPAIR_NAMED_WORKBOOK_DEFECT\": \"N32_WORKBOOK_TERMINALS\",\n148\t}\n149\t\n150\tSKELETON_NORMAL_EDGES: tuple[tuple[str, str], ...] = (\n151\t    (START, \"D00_BOOTSTRAP_EPISODE\"),\n152\t    (\"D96_GRACEFUL_INTERRUPT_GATE\", \"D98_WRITE_TERMINAL\"),\n153\t    (\"D98_WRITE_TERMINAL\", END),\n154\t)\n155\t\n156\tSKELETON_BRANCHES: tuple[tuple[str, Callable[[Mapping[str, Any]], str]], ...] = (\n157\t    (\"D00_BOOTSTRAP_EPISODE\", routing.route_bootstrap),\n158\t    (\"D01_VALIDATE_AND_FREEZE_INPUTS\", routing.route_frozen_inputs),\n159\t    (\"D02_COMPILE_EFFECTIVE_RUN\", routing.route_effective_run),\n160\t    (\"D00R_REVALIDATE_RESUME_IDENTITY\", routing.route_resume_identity),\n161\t    (\"D03_PROVE_CAPABILITIES\", routing.route_capabilities),\n162\t    (\"D04_INITIALIZE_OR_RESUME\", routing.route_initialize_or_resume),\n163\t)\n164\t\n165\t\n166\t# --------------------------------------------------------------- runtime context\n167\t\n168\t\n169\tdef _utc_clock() -> str:\n170\t    return datetime.now(timezone.utc).isoformat()\n171\t\n172\t\n173\tdef build_runtime_context(\n174\t    *,\n175\t    engine_root: Path | str,\n176\t    output_root: Path | str,\n177\t    run_id: str,\n178\t    curriculum_digest: str,\n179\t    authorization: Any = None,\n180\t    capability_proof: Mapping[str, Any] | None = None,\n181\t    retrieval_hosts: Sequence[str] = (),\n182\t    clock: Callable[[], Any] = _utc_clock,\n183\t    env_passthrough: Sequence[str] = (),\n184\t) -> RuntimeContext:\n185\t    \"\"\"Open the services one invocation may reach (spec section 5.2).\n186\t\n187\t    Constructed by the CLI after `prepare_episode_invocation` has fixed the run\n188\t    identity, and supplied to `invoke(context=...)`; it is deliberately not built\n189\t    inside the builder, because the transport and the authorization it enforces\n190\t    are bound to a run identity that does not exist at build time.\n191\t    \"\"\"\n192\t\n193\t    engine_root = Path(engine_root).resolve()\n194\t    output_root = Path(output_root).resolve()\n195\t    receipts = ReceiptLog(output_root / \".evidence\" / \"egress_receipts.jsonl\")\n196\t    egress_guard = EgressGuard(receipts)\n197\t    return RuntimeContext(\n198\t        engine_root=engine_root,\n199\t        output_root=output_root,\n200\t        path_guard=ArtifactStore(output_root),\n201\t        evidence_service=EvidenceStore(output_root),\n202\t        transport_registry=tp.CliTransport(\n203\t            output_root=output_root,\n204\t            run_id=run_id,\n205\t            curriculum_digest=curriculum_digest,\n206\t            authorization=authorization,\n207\t            receipts=receipts,\n208\t            guard=egress_guard,\n209\t            ledger=tp.AttemptLedger(),\n210\t            capability_proof=capability_proof,\n211\t            env_passthrough=env_passthrough,\n212\t        ),\n213\t        source_retriever=SourceRetriever(\n214\t            guard=egress_guard,\n215\t            policy=RetrievalPolicy(allowed_hosts=frozenset(retrieval_hosts)),\n216\t        ),\n217\t        signal_token=InterruptToken(output_root),\n218\t        clock=clock,\n219\t    )\n220\t\n221\t\n222\t# ----------------------------------------------------------------- node boundary\n223\t\n224\t\n225\tdef _mark_interrupt(update: Mapping[str, Any], node_id: str) -> dict[str, Any]:\n226\t    \"\"\"Record a graceful signal on the guard record so routing stays pure.\"\"\"\n227\t\n228\t    marked = dict(update)\n229\t    guard = marked.get(\"pending_guard\")\n230\t    guard = dict(guard) if isinstance(guard, Mapping) else {\"node\": node_id, \"value\": None}\n231\t    guard[\"interrupt_requested\"] = True\n232\t    marked[\"pending_guard\"] = guard\n233\t    return marked\n234\t\n235\t\n236\tdef _boundary(node_id: str, body: Callable[..., Any], *, model_node: bool) -> Callable[..., Any]:\n237\t    \"\"\"Wrap one node body in the common boundary of spec section 6.1.\n238\t\n239\t    LangGraph injects `Runtime`, not the opened services, so the boundary is also\n240\t    the only place the `RuntimeContext` reaches a node body — N22's and N23's\n241\t    callables take it as an explicit argument precisely so they cannot fetch it\n242\t    themselves.\n243\t    \"\"\"\n244\t\n245\t    def node(state: Mapping[str, Any], runtime: Runtime[RuntimeContext]) -> dict[str, Any]:\n246\t        context = getattr(runtime, \"context\", None)\n247\t        try:\n248\t            if model_node:\n249\t                update = body(state, build_model_node_context(context))\n250\t            else:\n251\t                update = body(state, context)\n252\t        except GraphBubbleUp:\n253\t            # LangGraph's own control flow (interrupt/resume propagation) is not a\n254\t            # product failure and must reach the engine untouched.\n255\t            raise\n256\t        except Exception as error:  # the classified-failure contract of spec 6.1\n257\t            return {\n258\t                \"pending_failure\": {\n259\t                    \"node\": node_id,\n260\t                    \"class\": \"system\",\n261\t                    \"cause\": \"unhandled\",\n262\t                    \"message\": f\"{type(error).__name__}: {error}\",\n263\t                    \"evidence\": {\"boundary\": \"node\"},\n264\t                },\n265\t                \"pending_guard\": None,\n266\t            }\n267\t        token = getattr(context, \"signal_token\", None)\n268\t        if token is not None and bool(getattr(token, \"is_set\", lambda: False)()):\n269\t            return _mark_interrupt(update, node_id)\n270\t        return dict(update)\n271\t\n272\t    node.__name__ = node_id\n273\t    node.__qualname__ = node_id\n274\t    node.__doc__ = getattr(body, \"__doc__\", None)\n275\t    node.plan26_binding = _binding_record(node_id, body)  # type: ignore[attr-defined]\n276\t    return node\n277\t\n278\t\n279\tdef _underlying(body: Callable[..., Any]) -> Callable[..., Any]:\n280\t    \"\"\"The authored function behind a decorated node, for identity and audit.\"\"\"\n281\t\n282\t    return getattr(body, \"node_body\", body)\n283\t\n284\t\n285\tdef _binding_record(node_id: str, body: Callable[..., Any]) -> dict[str, Any]:\n286\t    target = _underlying(body)\n287\t    try:\n288\t        source = inspect.getsource(target)\n289\t    except (OSError, TypeError):  # pragma: no cover - a source-less callable is rejected\n290\t        source = \"\"\n291\t    return {\n292\t        \"node_id\": node_id,\n293\t        \"module\": getattr(target, \"__module__\", \"\"),\n294\t        \"qualname\": getattr(target, \"__qualname__\", \"\"),\n295\t        \"source_sha256\": hashlib.sha256(source.encode(\"utf-8\")).hexdigest(),\n296\t        \"source_lines\": len(source.splitlines()),\n297\t    }\n298\t\n299\t\n300\t# ------------------------------------------------------------ binding validation\n301\t\n302\t\n303\tdef binding_inventory() -> dict[str, Callable[..., Any]]:\n304\t    \"\"\"Every node callable N20's own skeleton/unit-path tables resolve against.\n305\t\n306\t    N31's unit-repair-cycle nodes (D16-D23) carry no `NODE_CATALOGUE` row and\n307\t    are deliberately absent from *this* function's return value even though\n308\t    they are real, wired members of the compiled production graph: several of\n309\t    N30's own tests in `test_plan26_unit_graph.py` independently recompute\n310\t    their expectation directly from this function's return value, so it stays\n311\t    exactly what it was before N31 (per N90 finding F1's own resolution --\n312\t    `full_binding_inventory()`/`unit_repair_binding_inventory()` below are the\n313\t    functions that widen it; this one never does). Use `unit_repair_binding_\n314\t    inventory()` for the actual widened set `build_curriculum_factory_graph`\n315\t    compiles against.\n316\t\n317\t    N32's workbook engine (D24-D32, `workbook.WORKBOOK_NODE_BODIES`) is\n318\t    likewise absent from *this* function deliberately, not by oversight: D24\n319\t    is `D05_SELECT_NEXT_UNIT`'s own `manifest_exhausted` destination, and\n320\t    `unit_graph.DEFERRED_EDGES`/`unit_graph.UNIT_BRANCHES` (N30's frozen,\n321\t    already-verified tables) declare that edge deferred to N32 by name. If D24\n322\t    entered this function, `unit_graph.register_unit_path`'s *own*\n323\t    `available`-derived destination set for `D05_SELECT_NEXT_UNIT` would\n324\t    silently widen to include it -- correct for a production run, but it\n325\t    would falsify N30's own already-passing topology tests, which independently\n326\t    recompute their expectation from this exact function's return value.\n327\t    `register_workbook_topology` registers the workbook engine as an additive\n328\t    step over its own separate builder (N32 exercises it directly, not through\n329\t    `build_curriculum_factory_graph`), so the unit path's registered edges stay\n330\t    byte-identical to what they were before N32 and the workbook branch is\n331\t    still fully real -- just not reachable from `D05` in this generation,\n332\t    exactly as `unit_graph.DEFERRED_EDGES` documents.\n333\t    \"\"\"\n334\t\n335\t    bindings: dict[str, Callable[..., Any]] = dict(node_registry())\n336\t    for job_id, adapter in MODEL_NODE_ADAPTERS.items():\n337\t        bindings[job_id] = adapter\n338\t    bindings.update(MODEL_BOOKKEEPING_NODES)\n339\t    return bindings\n340\t\n341\t\n342\tdef unit_repair_binding_inventory() -> dict[str, Callable[..., Any]]:\n343\t    \"\"\"`binding_inventory()` plus this node's own D16-D23 unit-repair-cycle bodies.\n344\t\n345\t    The set `build_curriculum_factory_graph` actually compiles the one\n346\t    production graph against (N90 finding F1): D16-D23 become real, reachable\n347\t    members of that graph, while D24-D32 (N32's still-deferred workbook\n348\t    engine) stay absent, exactly as `binding_inventory()`'s own docstring\n349\t    documents for that pair. Kept separate from `binding_inventory()` itself\n350\t    so N30's tests, which recompute their expectation directly from that\n351\t    function's return value, stay unaffected by this widening.\n352\t    \"\"\"\n353\t\n354\t    bindings = dict(binding_inventory())\n355\t    bindings.update(acceptance.UNIT_REPAIR_NODE_BODIES)\n356\t    return bindings\n357\t\n358\t\n359\tdef full_binding_inventory() -> dict[str, Callable[..., Any]]:"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"2e2dab0f-1896-47a1-b9f2-90f9a7c4d3fd","uuid":"6985dfb5-e5c4-4624-aa97-97efbcde443f","timestamp":"2026-08-12T23:00:43.145Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/filipepinto/Projects/curriculum_builder/.plan26-run/plan26/attempts/N31_REPAIR_ACCEPTANCE/attempt-20260812T225852.833620Z-cb71442f0e/repo/runtime/langgraph_factory/graph.py","content":"    \"runtime.langgraph_factory.acceptance\",\n)\n\nPLACEHOLDER_NAME_MARKERS: tuple[str, ...] = (\n    \"stub\",\n    \"placeholder\",\n    \"fake\",\n    \"dummy\",\n    \"mock\",\n    \"sample\",\n    \"example\",\n    \"todo\",\n    \"noop\",\n    \"test\",\n)\n\nPLACEHOLDER_SOURCE_MARKERS: tuple[str, ...] = (\n    \"raise NotImplementedError\",\n    \"TODO: implement\",\n    \"placeholder implementation\",\n)\n\n# Registered here, wired by a later graph node. A node that is neither wired by\n# the skeleton/unit-path tables `_validate_topology` inspects nor declared here\n# fails the build: silence about an unwired node is how a topology gap becomes\n# a silent halt at runtime.\n#\n# D16 and D17 need no row: once their bodies are members of `available`, they\n# are reached as real *destinations* of already-wired `unit_graph.UNIT_BRANCHES`\n# sources (D08/D09/D12/D14/D91 -> D17, M05 -> D16 -- the six rows `unit_graph\n# .DEFERRED_EDGES` names), so `_validate_topology`'s own `wired` set already\n# contains them. D18-D23 are reached only from *inside* the unit repair cycle\n# itself (D17 -> D18 -> ... -> D21 -> D16, D22 -> D23 -> D05), which is wired by\n# `acceptance.register_unit_repair_path` (via `register_unit_repair_topology`,\n# called after `register_skeleton` returns) rather than by any table\n# `_validate_topology` reads -- so they are declared deferred here for the same\n# reason M06/M07/M08 are: really wired, by a registration step this function\n# does not itself see.\nDEFERRED_TOPOLOGY: Mapping[str, str] = {\n    \"D18_PLAN_TARGETED_UNIT_REPAIR\": \"N31_REPAIR_ACCEPTANCE\",\n    \"D19_ROUTE_UNIT_REPAIR\": \"N31_REPAIR_ACCEPTANCE\",\n    \"D20_ADMIT_UNIT_REPAIR\": \"N31_REPAIR_ACCEPTANCE\",\n    \"D21_RETEST_REQUIRED_DESCENDANTS\": \"N31_REPAIR_ACCEPTANCE\",\n    \"D22_ACCEPT_UNIT\": \"N31_REPAIR_ACCEPTANCE\",\n    \"D23_CHECKPOINT_ACCEPTED_UNIT\": \"N31_REPAIR_ACCEPTANCE\",\n    \"M06_REPAIR_NAMED_UNIT_ARTIFACT\": \"N31_REPAIR_ACCEPTANCE\",\n    \"M07_REVIEW_ACTUAL_WORKBOOK\": \"N32_WORKBOOK_TERMINALS\",\n    \"M08_REPAIR_NAMED_WORKBOOK_DEFECT\": \"N32_WORKBOOK_TERMINALS\",\n}\n\nSKELETON_NORMAL_EDGES: tuple[tuple[str, str], ...] = (\n    (START, \"D00_BOOTSTRAP_EPISODE\"),\n    (\"D96_GRACEFUL_INTERRUPT_GATE\", \"D98_WRITE_TERMINAL\"),\n    (\"D98_WRITE_TERMINAL\", END),\n)\n\nSKELETON_BRANCHES: tuple[tuple[str, Callable[[Mapping[str, Any]], str]], ...] = (\n    (\"D00_BOOTSTRAP_EPISODE\", routing.route_bootstrap),\n    (\"D01_VALIDATE_AND_FREEZE_INPUTS\", routing.route_frozen_inputs),\n    (\"D02_COMPILE_EFFECTIVE_RUN\", routing.route_effective_run),\n    (\"D00R_REVALIDATE_RESUME_IDENTITY\", routing.route_resume_identity),\n    (\"D03_PROVE_CAPABILITIES\", routing.route_capabilities),\n    (\"D04_INITIALIZE_OR_RESUME\", routing.route_initialize_or_resume),\n)\n\n\n# --------------------------------------------------------------- runtime context\n\n\ndef _utc_clock() -> str:\n    return datetime.now(timezone.utc).isoformat()\n\n\ndef build_runtime_context(\n    *,\n    engine_root: Path | str,\n    output_root: Path | str,\n    run_id: str,\n    curriculum_digest: str,\n    authorization: Any = None,\n    capability_proof: Mapping[str, Any] | None = None,\n    retrieval_hosts: Sequence[str] = (),\n    clock: Callable[[], Any] = _utc_clock,\n    env_passthrough: Sequence[str] = (),\n) -> RuntimeContext:\n    \"\"\"Open the services one invocation may reach (spec section 5.2).\n\n    Constructed by the CLI after `prepare_episode_invocation` has fixed the run\n    identity, and supplied to `invoke(context=...)`; it is deliberately not built\n    inside the builder, because the transport and the authorization it enforces\n    are bound to a run identity that does not exist at build time.\n    \"\"\"\n\n    engine_root = Path(engine_root).resolve()\n    output_root = Path(output_root).resolve()\n    receipts = ReceiptLog(output_root / \".evidence\" / \"egress_receipts.jsonl\")\n    egress_guard = EgressGuard(receipts)\n    return RuntimeContext(\n        engine_root=engine_root,\n        output_root=output_root,\n        path_guard=ArtifactStore(output_root),\n        evidence_service=EvidenceStore(output_root),\n        transport_registry=tp.CliTransport(\n            output_root=output_root,\n            run_id=run_id,\n            curriculum_digest=curriculum_digest,\n            authorization=authorization,\n            receipts=receipts,\n            guard=egress_guard,\n            ledger=tp.AttemptLedger(),\n            capability_proof=capability_proof,\n            env_passthrough=env_passthrough,\n        ),\n        source_retriever=SourceRetriever(\n            guard=egress_guard,\n            policy=RetrievalPolicy(allowed_hosts=frozenset(retrieval_hosts)),\n        ),\n        signal_token=InterruptToken(output_root),\n        clock=clock,\n    )\n\n\n# ----------------------------------------------------------------- node boundary\n\n\ndef _mark_interrupt(update: Mapping[str, Any], node_id: str) -> dict[str, Any]:\n    \"\"\"Record a graceful signal on the guard record so routing stays pure.\"\"\"\n\n    marked = dict(update)\n    guard = marked.get(\"pending_guard\")\n    guard = dict(guard) if isinstance(guard, Mapping) else {\"node\": node_id, \"value\": None}\n    guard[\"interrupt_requested\"] = True\n    marked[\"pending_guard\"] = guard\n    return marked\n\n\ndef _boundary(node_id: str, body: Callable[..., Any], *, model_node: bool) -> Callable[..., Any]:\n    \"\"\"Wrap one node body in the common boundary of spec section 6.1.\n\n    LangGraph injects `Runtime`, not the opened services, so the boundary is also\n    the only place the `RuntimeContext` reaches a node body — N22's and N23's\n    callables take it as an explicit argument precisely so they cannot fetch it\n    themselves.\n    \"\"\"\n\n    def node(state: Mapping[str, Any], runtime: Runtime[RuntimeContext]) -> dict[str, Any]:\n        context = getattr(runtime, \"context\", None)\n        try:\n            if model_node:\n                update = body(state, build_model_node_context(context))\n            else:\n                update = body(state, context)\n        except GraphBubbleUp:\n            # LangGraph's own control flow (interrupt/resume propagation) is not a\n            # product failure and must reach the engine untouched.\n            raise\n        except Exception as error:  # the classified-failure contract of spec 6.1\n            return {\n                \"pending_failure\": {\n                    \"node\": node_id,\n                    \"class\": \"system\",\n                    \"cause\": \"unhandled\",\n                    \"message\": f\"{type(error).__name__}: {error}\",\n                    \"evidence\": {\"boundary\": \"node\"},\n                },\n                \"pending_guard\": None,\n            }\n        token = getattr(context, \"signal_token\", None)\n        if token is not None and bool(getattr(token, \"is_set\", lambda: False)()):\n            return _mark_interrupt(update, node_id)\n        return dict(update)\n\n    node.__name__ = node_id\n    node.__qualname__ = node_id\n    node.__doc__ = getattr(body, \"__doc__\", None)\n    node.plan26_binding = _binding_record(node_id, body)  # type: ignore[attr-defined]\n    return node\n\n\ndef _underlying(body: Callable[..., Any]) -> Callable[..., Any]:\n    \"\"\"The authored function behind a decorated node, for identity and audit.\"\"\"\n\n    return getattr(body, \"node_body\", body)\n\n\ndef _binding_record(node_id: str, body: Callable[..., Any]) -> dict[str, Any]:\n    target = _underlying(body)\n    try:\n        source = inspect.getsource(target)\n    except (OSError, TypeError):  # pragma: no cover - a source-less callable is rejected\n        source = \"\"\n    return {\n        \"node_id\": node_id,\n        \"module\": getattr(target, \"__module__\", \"\"),\n        \"qualname\": getattr(target, \"__qualname__\", \"\"),\n        \"source_sha256\": hashlib.sha256(source.encode(\"utf-8\")).hexdigest(),\n        \"source_lines\": len(source.splitlines()),\n    }\n\n\n# ------------------------------------------------------------ binding validation\n\n\ndef binding_inventory() -> dict[str, Callable[..., Any]]:\n    \"\"\"Every node callable N20's own skeleton/unit-path tables resolve against.\n\n    N31's unit-repair-cycle nodes (D16-D23) carry no `NODE_CATALOGUE` row and\n    are deliberately absent from *this* function's return value even though\n    they are real, wired members of the compiled production graph: several of\n    N30's own tests in `test_plan26_unit_graph.py` independently recompute\n    their expectation directly from this function's return value, so it stays\n    exactly what it was before N31 (per N90 finding F1's own resolution --\n    `full_binding_inventory()`/`unit_repair_binding_inventory()` below are the\n    functions that widen it; this one never does). Use `unit_repair_binding_\n    inventory()` for the actual widened set `build_curriculum_factory_graph`\n    compiles against.\n\n    N32's workbook engine (D24-D32, `workbook.WORKBOOK_NODE_BODIES`) is\n    likewise absent from *this* function deliberately, not by oversight: D24\n    is `D05_SELECT_NEXT_UNIT`'s own `manifest_exhausted` destination, and\n    `unit_graph.DEFERRED_EDGES`/`unit_graph.UNIT_BRANCHES` (N30's frozen,\n    already-verified tables) declare that edge deferred to N32 by name. If D24\n    entered this function, `unit_graph.register_unit_path`'s *own*\n    `available`-derived destination set for `D05_SELECT_NEXT_UNIT` would\n    silently widen to include it -- correct for a production run, but it\n    would falsify N30's own already-passing topology tests, which independently\n    recompute their expectation from this exact function's return value.\n    `register_workbook_topology` registers the workbook engine as an additive\n    step over its own separate builder (N32 exercises it directly, not through\n    `build_curriculum_factory_graph`), so the unit path's registered edges stay\n    byte-identical to what they were before N32 and the workbook branch is\n    still fully real -- just not reachable from `D05` in this generation,\n    exactly as `unit_graph.DEFERRED_EDGES` documents.\n    \"\"\"\n\n    bindings: dict[str, Callable[..., Any]] = dict(node_registry())\n    for job_id, adapter in MODEL_NODE_ADAPTERS.items():\n        bindings[job_id] = adapter\n    bindings.update(MODEL_BOOKKEEPING_NODES)\n    return bindings\n\n\ndef unit_repair_binding_inventory() -> dict[str, Callable[..., Any]]:\n    \"\"\"`binding_inventory()` plus this node's own D16-D23 unit-repair-cycle bodies.\n\n    The set `build_curriculum_factory_graph` actually compiles the one\n    production graph against (N90 finding F1): D16-D23 become real, reachable\n    members of that graph, while D24-D32 (N32's still-deferred workbook\n    engine) stay absent, exactly as `binding_inventory()`'s own docstring\n    documents for that pair. Kept separate from `binding_inventory()` itself\n    so N30's tests, which recompute their expectation directly from that\n    function's return value, stay unaffected by this widening.\n    \"\"\"\n\n    bindings = dict(binding_inventory())\n    bindings.update(acceptance.UNIT_REPAIR_NODE_BODIES)\n    return bindings\n\n\ndef full_binding_inventory() -> dict[str, Callable[..., Any]]:","numLines":260,"startLine":100,"totalLines":643}}}
