{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5","id":"msg_011CdygspjiSKovfhtRw9L6V","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01QYNB6oD9E5bKWf91VRmacx","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/Users/filipepinto/Projects/curriculum_builder/.plan26-run/plan26/attempts/N31_REPAIR_ACCEPTANCE/attempt-20260812T225852.833620Z-cb71442f0e/repo/plans/26_langgraph_curriculum_factory/results/N31_REPAIR_ACCEPTANCE.result.v1.md","content":"# N31_REPAIR_ACCEPTANCE result\n\nstatus: PASSED\nnode_prompt: plans/26_langgraph_curriculum_factory/prompts/N31_repair_acceptance.prompt.v2.md\npredecessor: N30_UNIT_GRAPH (compact state supplied by the controller, status PASSED)\ngeneration: 4\nactive_patches: P-N31-001, P-N31-002, P-N31-003\n\n## What this node built\n\nTwo new top-level modules, per `contracts/node_ownership.v1.md` (\"N31 owns\nrepair/acceptance modules, not terminal.py\"):\n\n- `runtime/langgraph_factory/repair.py` — D17 (finding classification), D18\n  (targeted repair planning), D19 (deterministic-vs-model routing), D20\n  (boundary-checked admission), D21 (retest dispatch).\n- `runtime/langgraph_factory/acceptance.py` — D16 (unit denominator\n  reduction), D22 (recompute-and-accept), D23 (checkpoint correlation +\n  cursor advance), plus `prove_exact_manifest_coverage()`, the D24 coverage\n  predicate N32 will call, plus (as of P-N31-001) `register_unit_repair_path`/\n  `register_unit_repair_topology`, which wire D16-D23's internal edges.\n- `runtime/langgraph_factory/graph.py` (as of P-N31-001, closing N90's\n  finding F1 — see below) now compiles D16-D23 into the one production\n  graph via `unit_repair_binding_inventory()`/`full_binding_inventory()` and\n  `register_unit_repair_topology()`, called from `build_curriculum_factory_\n  graph()` after `register_skeleton`/`register_unit_path`/`register_workbook_\n  topology`.\n\n`tests/runtime/test_plan26_repair_acceptance.py` calls every D17-D23 function\ndirectly against hand-built `FactoryState` fixtures, merged step-to-step\nthrough the real field reducers (`state.FIELD_REDUCERS`), not a mock merge,\nand (P-N31-001) additionally drives the real compiled production graph\nend to end through `_HarnessContext`/`mn.tp.FakeCliTransport`, the same\nscripted-transport pattern `test_plan26_adversarial.py` established.\n\n## P-N31-001 correction: D16-D23 wired into the compiled production graph\n\nN90's independent audit (finding F1) found D16-D23 fully implemented and\nfunction-level tested, but never registered into `build_curriculum_factory_\ngraph()`, because this node's own `repair.py` docstring deferred wiring to\nN32, whose own prompt deferred it right back — nobody wired the unit repair\ncycle into the one production compile point, so no real run could ever reach\n`D22_ACCEPT_UNIT`/`UNIT_ACCEPTED`.\n\n`graph.py` is now in this node's write set to close that gap directly.\nFixed, per the patch's own instructions:\n\n- `unit_graph.py` (N30's frozen module) is untouched. Once D16-D23's bodies\n  are members of the `available` sequence `register_unit_path` sees, the six\n  `unit_graph.DEFERRED_EDGES` rows this node owns resolve automatically —\n  `unit_graph.py` was already built for exactly this widening.\n- `graph.py`'s existing `binding_inventory()` return value is byte-for-byte\n  unchanged (`test_binding_inventory_return_value_is_unchanged_by_this_\n  nodes_wiring`, in `tests/runtime/test_plan26_repair_acceptance.py`,\n  independently diffs it against the widened set). N30's own tests in\n  `tests/runtime/test_plan26_unit_graph.py`, which recompute their\n  expectations directly from that function's return value, keep passing\n  unmodified. The wider set `build_curriculum_factory_graph()` actually\n  compiles against is `unit_repair_binding_inventory()` (`binding_\n  inventory()` + `acceptance.UNIT_REPAIR_NODE_BODIES`) /\n  `full_binding_inventory()` (that, plus the workbook bindings N32 already\n  added) — the same pattern N32 used for the workbook engine.\n- `acceptance.register_unit_repair_path`/`graph.register_unit_repair_\n  topology` wire D16-D23's internal loop (D17→D18→D19→[deterministic\n  producer, or D90→M06]→D20→D21→earliest invalidated producer/check→D16;\n  D16 PASS→D22→D23→D05; D17/D18 repeat/attempt-bound exhaustion→D98) as an\n  additive registration step over the builder `register_skeleton`/`register_\n  unit_path` already populated — the same worked pattern as `workbook.\n  register_workbook_path`/`graph.register_workbook_topology`.\n- `workbook.py`, `unit_graph.py`, and D24-D32 are untouched, per the patch's\n  explicit instruction not to restore or duplicate N32's write.\n\nRequired proof, executed against the real compiled graph (`plans/26_\nlanggraph_curriculum_factory/results/evidence/N31_REPAIR_ACCEPTANCE/\ncompiled_graph_topology.txt`):\n\n- D16-D23 (and M06) are members of `build_curriculum_factory_graph(...)\n  .get_graph().nodes` — all `True`.\n- The six N31-owned `DEFERRED_EDGES` rows are now real, wired edges in the\n  compiled graph — all `wired=True`.\n- `binding_inventory()` stays disjoint from `UNIT_REPAIR_NODE_BODIES` —\n  confirmed `True`.\n- `tests/runtime/test_plan26_repair_acceptance.py::\n  test_a_clean_one_unit_episode_reaches_d22_accept_unit_via_the_d16_pass_\n  fast_path` and `::test_a_full_d17_through_d21_repair_and_retest_loop_\n  reaches_d22_accept_unit` drive the real compiled graph through\n  `_HarnessContext`/`mn.tp.FakeCliTransport` and assert `D22_ACCEPT_UNIT`\n  (and, for the second, the full D17-D21 loop back to D16) in `result[\n  \"trace\"]` — both pass.\n- `tests/runtime/test_plan26_repair_acceptance.py::test_widening_the_\n  bindings_raises_no_topology_or_binding_error` confirms `register_skeleton`\n  raises no `UnitTopologyError`/`GraphBindingError` against the widened\n  bindings.\n\nBoth `repair.py`'s and `acceptance.py`'s module docstrings, which N90 quoted\nas the root cause (each said registration was \"N32's write\"), are corrected\nthis generation to describe the real, wired state instead.\n\n## P-N31-002 / P-N31-003 correction: status line and two residual unit_graph.py failures\n\nP-N31-002: an earlier generation's report opened with a multi-line `status:\nPASSED (...)` line the controller's `^status:\\s*(PASSED|NOT_AVAILABLE|\nBLOCKED)\\s*$` parser could not match. That generation also reported the two\ntests below as failing, produced by this node's own D16-D23 wiring landing\noutside its write set at the time, and correctly declined to force a\nmisleading `PASSED` status. This report's status line is now the required\nbare form, and both residual failures are closed (P-N31-003, `tests/runtime/\ntest_plan26_unit_graph.py` now in this node's write set specifically for\nthese two):\n\n1. `test_the_unobservable_boundary_is_excluded_for_a_stated_reason` — its own\n   docstring predicted this exact inversion: once `D16_REDUCE_UNIT_EVIDENCE`\n   became a real wired node body, M05's update is no longer swallowed by a\n   deferred destination and reaches the stream like any other boundary's\n   update. The test now asserts that inversion directly (M05's stream chunk\n   is real and non-empty; its receipt/candidate/review are still committed)\n   instead of the retired pre-wiring exclusion. `REACHABLE_BOUNDARIES`/\n   `UNOBSERVABLE_BOUNDARY` are untouched, since other tests still rely on\n   them.\n2. `test_a_fresh_episode_executes_the_bootstrap_spine_once_through_\n   langgraph` — a real, reproducible LangGraph `stream(stream_mode=\n   \"updates\")` artifact: the chunk for a step whose *next* step's routing\n   raises in the same tick is never yielded, so the second `D05_SELECT_\n   NEXT_UNIT` call (which correctly finds the manifest exhausted and routes\n   to the still-deferred `D24_PROVE_EXACT_MANIFEST_COVERAGE`) is real and\n   really checkpoints (`cursor.accepted_ordinal`, cleared `selected_unit_id`)\n   but is swallowed by the same-tick `KeyError` before `result[\"trace\"]`\n   records it, undercounting the `D05` trace count by exactly one. The test\n   now asserts the real, checkpointed final state directly (`state[\n   \"selected_unit_id\"] is None`, `state[\"cursor\"][\"accepted_ordinal\"] == 1`)\n   instead of inferring the outcome from a trace count this specific stream/\n   exception interaction cannot reliably produce. `compiled.stream()`'s\n   call, mode, and `graph.py`/`unit_graph.py` are untouched — only the\n   test's own assertion changed.\n\nBoth required verification commands are re-run against the current\nrepository state and are fully green: `test_plan26_repair_acceptance.py`\n38/38 passed; `test_plan26_unit_graph.py` 93/93 passed (see Commands below).\nNo other test in `test_plan26_unit_graph.py` — including the five P-N30-001\nalready corrected — was touched.\n\n## Owner / retest map\n\n| Owner | Channel | Repair route (this generation) | First retest node |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| source interpretation | domain | model (M06) | `D07_CORRELATE_AND_ADMIT_SOURCES` |\n| curriculum domain | domain | model (M06) | `D08_VALIDATE_DOMAIN` |\n| unit content | content | model (M06) | `D09_VALIDATE_CONTENT` |\n| unit visual | visuals | model (M06) unless every named key is an authoritative/library brief, then deterministic | `D10_COMPILE_VISUAL_BRIEFS` |\n| unit layout | layout | deterministic (boundary-scoped pointer correction) | `D13_RENDER_UNIT` |\n\n`repair.RETEST_ORDER_BY_OWNER` carries each owner's full fixed chain (spec\nsection 12's table); D21 dispatches only the first node of that chain — the\nremaining steps are the already-wired unit-path edges (N30) that node's own\nsuccess guard reaches on its own, so D21 is never re-entered for the same\nrepair admission.\n\nFrozen limits, enforced exactly where spec section 6.2 assigns them: D17\nowns the repeated-fingerprint bound (`MAX_FINGERPRINT_REPEATS = 2`); D18 owns\nthe numeric attempt bound (`MAX_REPAIR_CHILDREN_PER_CHAIN = 3`).\n\n## Denominator trace (D16 / D22, `acceptance.compute_unit_denominator`)\n\nRecomputed identically by D16 (before repair) and D22 (immediately before\nminting an accepted receipt) off whatever heads are *current* at call time.\nCategories enforced this generation: source admission (sha256-resolved),\ndomain check set (`DOMAIN_CHECK_IDS`, matched by current head hash), content\ncheck set (`CONTENT_CHECK_IDS`, matched by current head hash), visual join\nresult, page inventory + inspection set (exact page count, all PASS), one\nindependent unit review with every blocking finding's `category` mapped\nthrough the code-owned `owner_for_review_category()` table (never trusted\nverbatim from the model), and repair-request closure (no request left\nunresolved). `test_removing_or_failing_any_single_member_makes_d22_reject`\nindependently removes/fails each of the five owner-bearing categories and\nconfirms D22 raises every time; `test_staling_the_content_head_makes_d22_reject`\nconfirms a check recorded against a superseded head is invisible to the\nreduction (stale evidence cannot pass) without needing to delete anything —\n`compute_unit_denominator` only counts a check whose `head_hash` equals the\n*current* head.\n\nDocumented, not silently assumed, scope limit: this generation's denominator\ntreats the append-only evidence/log layer and the LangGraph checkpoint layer\nas structurally present (state reducers already enforce their shape) rather\nthan independently re-auditing their hash chain from inside D22 (spec\nsection 13.1 items 13-14). `acceptance.py`'s module docstring records this so\na future generation tightens it rather than rediscovering the gap.\n\n## Real-D98 traces (TEST 9)\n\n`tests/runtime/test_plan26_repair_acceptance.py` imports\n`runtime.langgraph_factory.nodes.terminal` unmodified and calls\n`terminal.write_terminal()` directly — the identical function N22 wrote and\nN32 will call for its two product-terminal sites — never a stand-in:\n\n- `test_a_unit_accepted_candidate_traverses_the_real_d98_and_is_accepted`:\n  a `UNIT_ACCEPTED` candidate built from this generation's real D22/D23\n  output is independently re-derived and accepted by D98's own\n  `_validate_unit_accepted`.\n- `test_a_tampered_unit_accepted_candidate_is_rejected_by_the_real_d98`: the\n  same candidate with a forged `receipt_hash` is rejected and D98 writes\n  `SYSTEM_FAILURE` in its place — no N31 code decided that; D98's own\n  re-derivation did.\n- `test_a_convergence_exhausted_candidate_from_d17_traverses_the_real_d98`:\n  the `terminal_candidate` D18 proposes on attempt-bound exhaustion is\n  independently accepted by D98's `_validate_exhausted`.\n\nNo test in this file, and no code in `repair.py`/`acceptance.py`, writes to\n`nodes/terminal.py`; `terminal.write_terminal.__module__` is asserted to\nstill be `runtime.langgraph_factory.nodes.terminal`.\n\n## Commands and results\n\n```\n/tmp/plan26_n30_verify/bin/python -m pytest -q tests/runtime/test_plan26_repair_acceptance.py\n=> 38 passed in 0.80s\n\n/tmp/plan26_n30_verify/bin/python -m pytest -q tests/runtime/test_plan26_unit_graph.py\n=> 93 passed in 6.80s\n\n/tmp/plan26_n30_verify/bin/python -m pytest tests/runtime/test_plan26_repair_acceptance.py tests/runtime/test_plan26_unit_graph.py -v\n=> 131 passed in 7.38s\n(results/evidence/N31_REPAIR_ACCEPTANCE/focused_test_run.txt)\n\n/tmp/plan26_n30_verify/bin/python -m pytest tests/runtime/ -k plan26 -q\n=> 1 failed, 1066 passed, 1 skipped, 174 deselected, 345 subtests passed\n(results/evidence/N31_REPAIR_ACCEPTANCE/full_plan26_suite.txt)\n```\n\nThe 1 failure is `test_plan26_prompt_graph_controller.py::\ntest_passed_nodes_remain_admissible_after_harness_or_predecessor_change`,\nasserting `N20_GRAPH_COMPILER` receipt admissibility off `results/v3/*.\nreceipt.v1.json`/`results/v3/logs/**` evidence-directory state that is\noutside this node's declared writable paths (`prompt_graph_controller.py`\nand receipt files are not in N31's write set) and outside both of this\nnode's own required verification commands. Not a regression this node\nintroduced: `repair.py`, `acceptance.py`, `graph.py`, and the two test files\nthis node writes do not touch that controller or any receipt file.\n\n## Compiled-graph evidence (P-N31-001)\n\n```\n=== D16-D23 + M06 present in compiled nodes ===\nD16_REDUCE_UNIT_EVIDENCE True\nD17_CLASSIFY_UNIT_FINDINGS True\nD18_PLAN_TARGETED_UNIT_REPAIR True\nD19_ROUTE_UNIT_REPAIR True\nD20_ADMIT_UNIT_REPAIR True\nD21_RETEST_REQUIRED_DESCENDANTS True\nD22_ACCEPT_UNIT True\nD23_CHECKPOINT_ACCEPTED_UNIT True\nM06_REPAIR_NAMED_UNIT_ARTIFACT True\n\n=== The six N31-owned unit_graph.DEFERRED_EDGES rows, now real edges ===\nD08_VALIDATE_DOMAIN --[domain_repairable]--> D17_CLASSIFY_UNIT_FINDINGS  wired=True\nD09_VALIDATE_CONTENT --[content_repairable]--> D17_CLASSIFY_UNIT_FINDINGS  wired=True\nD12_VISUAL_BARRIER_AND_JOIN --[visuals_repairable]--> D17_CLASSIFY_UNIT_FINDINGS  wired=True\nD14_INVENTORY_AND_INSPECT_UNIT_PAGES --[layout_repairable]--> D17_CLASSIFY_UNIT_FINDINGS  wired=True\nD91_CLASSIFY_MODEL_FAILURE --[repair]--> D17_CLASSIFY_UNIT_FINDINGS  wired=True\nM05_REVIEW_ACTUAL_UNIT --[review_returned]--> D16_REDUCE_UNIT_EVIDENCE  wired=True\n\n=== binding_inventory() unchanged (no D16-D23 members) ===\ndisjoint from UNIT_REPAIR_NODE_BODIES: True\n\n=== graph digest (self-consistency) ===\n53790bb433dde844e19c0bd0e6998801d3d638a89922acc7bc5ecafdf3c27b27\nnode count: 42 edge count: 137\n```\n(results/evidence/N31_REPAIR_ACCEPTANCE/compiled_graph_topology.txt)\n\n## Hashes\n\n| File | SHA-256 (shasum -a 256) |\n|---|---|\n| `runtime/langgraph_factory/repair.py` | `589f1826ecf90414708f8be445ec16dd85391c633e02fdb36dff6cecc482f008` |\n| `runtime/langgraph_factory/acceptance.py` | `97f36121609c2c449a5f6caa4bf66a74f226c338abe51e9985fd2a74eba0b8b6` |\n| `runtime/langgraph_factory/graph.py` | `efabbd515c4ba2aab811e47a88ac2ffe2742a23fec9b7e46060ec7e385f06aaa` |\n| `tests/runtime/test_plan26_repair_acceptance.py` | `de6552e7f6d419405ae2cceb619087cc07bf358cc72a6a0