test_re_admitting_the_same_repair_after_the_head_already_advanced_fails_closed`,\n    `test_a_crash_before_the_terminal_write_still_lets_d98_be_invoked_cleanly`.\n\nP-N31-001 required proof (see \"Compiled-graph evidence\" above and \"P-N31-001\ncorrection\"): **PASSED** —\n`test_d16_through_d23_and_m06_are_members_of_the_compiled_production_graph`,\n`test_binding_inventory_return_value_is_unchanged_by_this_nodes_wiring`,\n`test_the_six_n31_owned_deferred_edges_are_now_real_wired_edges`,\n`test_widening_the_bindings_raises_no_topology_or_binding_error`,\n`test_a_clean_one_unit_episode_reaches_d22_accept_unit_via_the_d16_pass_fast_path`,\n`test_a_full_d17_through_d21_repair_and_retest_loop_reaches_d22_accept_unit`.\n\n## Known scope limitations (for N32 and future generations)\n\n- The deterministic-vs-model routing table for `source interpretation` is\n  simplified to always route to M06 in this generation; spec section 12\n  allows a deterministic refetch when a locator remains authorized, which\n  would require a source-retrieval integration this node's write set does\n  not include (`repair.py`'s module docstring records the reasoning).\n- `compute_unit_denominator()`'s coverage of spec section 13.1 items 13-14\n  (append-log/evidence-index and checkpoint/state-digest integrity) is\n  structural, not a byte-level hash-chain re-audit from inside D22.\n- D16-D23 are wired into the compiled production graph (P-N31-001); D24-D32\n  (workbook branch) registration remains N32's write, per\n  `implementation.graph.v3.yaml` and `contracts/node_ownership.v1.md`. This\n  generation does not touch `workbook.py` or `unit_graph.py`.\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2348,"cache_read_input_tokens":82099,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2348},"output_tokens":7,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"dia